# Output of `cargo run --example model_card_example`, which writes into the
# REPOSITORY ROOT. Six such files were committed with v0.1.0 and removed in
# PR #33; without these entries the next run re-creates them and `git add .`
# re-commits them -- a deletion with a scheduled recurrence.
#
# Root-anchored and underscore-prefixed on purpose: `README.md` and
# `CONTRIBUTING.md` do not match, and nothing under a subdirectory does.
/*_README.md
/*_model_card.json

# Output of `cargo run --example onnx_export_example`, which writes into the
# REPOSITORY ROOT. Committed once and removed in the third documentation pass;
# `ONNX_SUPPORT.md` DESCRIBES the example creating it rather than depending on
# the committed copy, so nothing reads it. Same reasoning as the
# `*_model_card.json` entries above: a deletion without an ignore is a fix
# with a scheduled recurrence.
/test_transformer.onnx
